.TH WBAR 1
.SH NAME
wbar \- the desktop's bar in wsys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wbar
[
.B -m
.I menu
] [
.B -f
.I font.ttf
] [
.B -s
.I size
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Wbar
runs in a window of
.IR wsys (4)
and makes it a bar along the top of the screen
(the
.B bar
message to
.BR /dev/wctl :
no border, above the other windows, the mouse but never the keyboard's focus;
a window maximized stays below it).
On it are, from the start:
.TP
.B menu
Button 1 opens a menu below the bar, held (let go on an item) or clicked
(a click on an item, anywhere else shuts it); it is
.IR wsys 's
(the window's
.B menu
file), as wide as its items.
An item runs its command with
.IR rc (1)
in
.IR wbar 's
name space: its
.B /dev
is its window's,
.IR window (1)
makes a new window.
The items are the lines of
.I menu
(default
.BR $home/lib/wbar/menu ,
else
.BR /lib/wbar/menu ):
a label, a tab, the command; lines starting with
.B #
are comments.
.TP
the windows
of
.B /dev/wsys
by number, each by its label (else
.BI window " n\f1),"
cut to fit: the current one on the theme's selection colour, a hidden one paler.
Button 1 on one makes it current; on the current one, it hides it; on a hidden
one, it brings it back.
.TP
a clock
at the end: the local time from
.IR date (1),
weekday, day, month, hours and minutes.
.PP
The colours are the theme's
.RB ( /dev/theme ,
.IR wsys (4)):
.B window
behind,
.B text
for the text,
.B border
for a line at the bottom and the menu's frame,
.B menuhigh
for the item under the mouse.
The font is
.IR font.ttf ,
else the theme's
.BR uifont ,
else
.BR /lib/font/ttf/Go-Regular.ttf ,
.I size
pixels (15).
When
.I wsys
says the window changed, it reads the theme again.
It looks at the windows twice a second.
.PP
.IR Riostart ,
under
.I wsys
.RB ( desktop=wsys ),
starts it first.
.SH EXAMPLES
A menu of one's own:
.IP
.EX
term	window term
mail	window -r 100 100 700 600 acme /mail/fs/mbox
theme: modern	cat /lib/theme/modern >/dev/theme
.EE
.SH FILES
.TF /lib/wbar/menu
.TP
.B /lib/wbar/menu
the menu by default
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/wbar
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR wsys (4),
.IR winwatch (1),
.IR window (1),
.IR term (1)
.SH BUGS
Under
.IR rio (1),
which knows no bars, it is an ordinary window.
.br
.B WBARDEBUG=items
writes where things are on the bar (and whether the menu is open) to
.BI /tmp/wbar. pid .items
after each picture (for tests).
